    "content": "As of March 23, 2026, a major recall affects nearly 10 million pounds of Trader Joe's frozen foods—specifically Vegetable Fried Rice, Chicken Fried Rice, Japanese Style Fried Rice, and Chicken Shu Mai—due to potential contamination with glass fragments. These items were sold in 43 states with best-buy dates in 2026-2027. Key Details for Consumers (As of March 2026): Affected Products: Trader Joe’s Vegetable Fried Rice, Chicken Fried Rice, Japanese Style Fried Rice, and Chicken Shu Mai dumplings. Reason: Possible presence of \"foreign objects,\" specifically hard, clear glass (1–3 cm long) from a vegetable ingredient. Best-Buy Dates: Affected products have dates ranging between Feb. 28, 2026, and Aug. 19, 2027 (some reports mention October 2026 for specific items). Action: Check your freezer. If you have these products, do not eat them. Return them to any Trader Joe's location for a full refund or throw them away. The recall, initiated by Ajinomoto Foods North America Inc., is a significant expansion of earlier safety alerts, involving products distributed nationwide to 43 states, excluding only Hawaii, Maine, New Mexico, South Dakota, Vermont, West Virginia, and Iowa. For the most up-to-date information, check the official Trader Joe's Product Recalls page and the FDA database.",
